WEBVTT

00:13.000 --> 00:14.666
Well, it happened in

00:14.666 --> 00:16.366
the night of Friday and Saturday.

00:16.366 --> 00:19.100
I woke up by the sound

00:19.100 --> 00:21.533
of breaking glass
in my house,

00:21.666 --> 00:23.233
in my bedroom.

00:23.233 --> 00:24.800
I suddenly
realized that

00:24.800 --> 00:25.866
there was a heat,

00:26.200 --> 00:28.233
an enormous
heat in my room.

00:29.333 --> 00:31.633
At the beginning, I thought that my son had put up the

00:31.633 --> 00:33.566
temperature in the house.

00:33.600 --> 00:37.333
Then I realized that there was a fire downstairs.

00:37.466 --> 00:41.733
I immediately got up, but I realized that I couldn't get

00:41.733 --> 00:43.266
out of my bedroom.

00:43.666 --> 00:48.033
The road, way to the stairs, was blocked because of the

00:48.033 --> 00:52.466
heat. I jumped to the floor because there is a small part

00:52.466 --> 00:57.533
of oxygen on the floor, and I started crawling in the dark

00:57.800 --> 00:59.833
smoke looking for the window.

01:00.766 --> 01:02.200
I couldn't find my window.

01:02.466 --> 01:05.633
It's my own bedroom, but I couldn't find my own window.

01:07.000 --> 01:08.300
I panicked a little bit.

01:09.133 --> 01:10.666
There was so much heat.

01:10.666 --> 01:15.400
I found my window, and I realized that I should be very

01:15.400 --> 01:17.266
careful in opening the window.

01:17.900 --> 01:22.233
Because when oxygen enters and there's such a heat and

01:22.533 --> 01:24.033
there might be an explosion.

01:24.533 --> 01:27.066
So little by little, I opened that window.

01:28.133 --> 01:31.800
So I got out in my underwear with no shoes.

01:32.633 --> 01:34.533
I got on the roof of my house.

01:34.600 --> 01:38.900
Luckily, I have a ladder on the roof and so I could escape

01:39.333 --> 01:41.033
from the roof to my garden.

01:41.066 --> 01:45.066
I ran to the street to alert the neighbors because I didn't

01:45.066 --> 01:46.333
have a phone with me.

01:46.333 --> 01:51.466
Because I realized also that as long as I cannot alert the

01:51.466 --> 01:53.433
rescue service of the fire brigade,

01:54.033 --> 01:55.300
then I would be on my own.

01:55.333 --> 01:58.100
Luckily for me, they immediately responded.

01:58.100 --> 02:01.833
I went back because my son was still in the house,

02:01.833 --> 02:04.000
I thought. I knocked on his window,

02:04.500 --> 02:05.866
but there was no reaction.

02:06.466 --> 02:09.866
Then I realized I had to put out a fire myself,

02:10.300 --> 02:14.933
which I did. But then even by putting out a fire,

02:15.266 --> 02:17.133
it was too hot to enter.

02:17.133 --> 02:19.666
And there was all. Everywhere was glass.

02:19.666 --> 02:21.966
Broken glass. With my bare foot,

02:22.033 --> 02:23.366
I couldn't enter.

02:24.033 --> 02:25.866
So I decided to break in.

02:25.900 --> 02:27.533
In the glass of his bedroom.

02:27.566 --> 02:33.866
The window. When I saw the smoke and I felt the heat and I

02:33.866 --> 02:35.166
saw that his bed was empty.

02:35.166 --> 02:38.866
And then I panicked immediately because I thought he ran

02:38.866 --> 02:43.166
away in the wrong direction, and that I would discover him

02:43.166 --> 02:45.566
somewhere on the floor, dead.

02:45.566 --> 02:48.466
But then I realized that the day before,

02:48.733 --> 02:51.466
I dropped him off at the Boy Scout weekend,

02:51.466 --> 02:54.566
so I was extremely happy.

03:03.966 --> 03:06.633
It's only afterwards that I realized what was the cause of

03:06.633 --> 03:11.033
the fire, and it was a battery that was charging during the

03:11.033 --> 03:15.933
night and that battery exploded during the night.

03:16.300 --> 03:22.300
So that explosion has set fire everywhere in my house.

03:22.600 --> 03:28.966
So let's say that that everything in in a circle of 15m

03:28.966 --> 03:33.400
around that battery melted, was burned down.

03:33.433 --> 03:37.800
A lot of heat, which is typical for the battery explosion.

03:37.833 --> 03:39.600
The medics, they took care of me.

03:40.166 --> 03:41.766
They brought me to the hospital.

03:41.800 --> 03:42.900
They examined me.

03:42.933 --> 03:46.900
I had some smoke inhalation, but luckily,

03:46.933 --> 03:49.033
me, it was quite all right.

03:49.300 --> 03:55.733
Trauma. This is an experience that is

03:56.766 --> 03:58.566
quite hard, even for me.

03:58.600 --> 04:01.166
I'm a trained journalist.

04:01.166 --> 04:05.933
I've been in, in, in, in, in Africa in very difficult and

04:05.933 --> 04:07.533
dangerous situations.

04:08.000 --> 04:09.766
But this, this happened in my,

04:10.033 --> 04:14.900
my own house, where in fact I'm very familiar with the

04:14.900 --> 04:16.466
house, especially there.

04:17.000 --> 04:20.866
It's it's like an an attack on your,

04:20.866 --> 04:25.533
your personal on your life, but also intimacy.

04:26.533 --> 04:28.066
That's a, that's a rough one.

04:37.500 --> 04:40.600
Well, in my house we have several smoke alarms.

04:40.800 --> 04:41.933
I didn't hear them.

04:41.933 --> 04:45.700
And the reason why is that after the fire,

04:46.433 --> 04:49.900
we examined the place and we found the smoke alarms.

04:50.500 --> 04:53.800
They were all melted. As a precaution for the future.

04:55.800 --> 04:59.000
I will install in my house smoke alarms.

04:59.333 --> 05:01.333
But that are in connection with each other.

05:01.400 --> 05:05.733
That even if there is a fire far away from your bedroom

05:06.533 --> 05:09.700
within your house or in your your cellar or whatever,

05:10.133 --> 05:16.266
that all the smoke alarms in your house will start ringing

05:16.266 --> 05:21.066
or buzzing or making a sound so that you will be alerted

05:21.066 --> 05:22.300
that there is a problem.

05:22.333 --> 05:25.466
What saved me because it was a real close call.

05:25.700 --> 05:29.766
It shouldn't have taken more than than a couple of seconds

05:29.766 --> 05:31.966
later I would have been dead.

05:32.033 --> 05:35.866
The smoke was enormous and the heat.

05:36.166 --> 05:41.900
And if I hadn't heard the sound of the breaking glass,

05:42.900 --> 05:46.266
I probably would have died in my sleep.

05:46.500 --> 05:47.966
But I woke up.

05:48.833 --> 05:52.766
What saved me is probably the training that I had in the

05:52.766 --> 05:55.533
past because of my profession.

05:55.533 --> 05:59.400
But even even though with that training it was a difficult one.

06:05.666 --> 06:08.966
I have two advices. That's one.

06:09.233 --> 06:14.066
Don't charge your battery in your house and don't charge it

06:14.066 --> 06:15.966
when you're when you're going to sleep.

06:16.733 --> 06:19.566
I think it's a, it's a precaution

06:19.600 --> 06:20.733
Don't do that.

06:21.600 --> 06:28.000
And secondly, put smoke alarms in your house and make sure

06:28.000 --> 06:32.933
that these alarms are in connection with each other so that

06:32.933 --> 06:36.700
if one goes off, all the rest goes off,

06:36.700 --> 06:41.366
and that you even if you are ten meters away on another

06:41.533 --> 06:43.400
floor, that you will hear it,

06:43.400 --> 06:45.733
that you will be saved by the bell,

06:45.733 --> 06:47.533
by the alert.

06:53.366 --> 06:56.500
I’m okay. This is some time ago now.

06:56.733 --> 07:03.166
Every time when you hear that someone else has not survived

07:03.200 --> 07:06.700
the fire in the house, it makes you think that what

07:06.700 --> 07:09.766
happened to me, that I was extremely lucky.

07:09.933 --> 07:14.433
It makes you also think about the advice that should go out

07:14.600 --> 07:16.566
with a lot of pressure to the people,

07:16.566 --> 07:20.166
like put these smoke alarms in the house.
